<title>KUWAIT: Kuwait Feb bank assets rise month/month, yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Kuwait Feb bank assets rise month/month, yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Combined assets of banks operating in Kuwait rose to 11.749 billion dinars at the end of February from 11.493 billion at the end of January, central bank said in a monthly bulletin.</p>
<p>Assets were 11.317 billion dinars in February 1996.</p>
<p>			Figures in million Kuwaiti dinars</p>
<p>						Feb '97	   Feb '96</p>
<p> Cash					  81.0		 52.9</p>
<p> Balances with Central Bank	     4.5		  5.2</p>
<p> Public debt instruments	    1,722.8	    2,008.6</p>
<p> Debt purchase bonds		  2,744.6	    3,351.6</p>
<p> Other local investments		284.9		358.2</p>
<p>Credit facilities to</p>
<p>  residents			     3,341.8	    2,469.1</p>
<p> Foreign assets			 2,235.9	    2,054.9</p>
<p> Inter bank local deposits	    749.5		542.2</p>
<p> Other assets			     583.9		474.5</p>
<p> Total				   11,748.9	   11,317.2</p>
<p>Note: Data covers eight commercial and specialised banks, the Islamic institution Kuwait Finance House and a Kuwaiti branch of a Bahrain-based bank.</p>
<p>Debt purchase bonds include the value of the purchase by the government of the real estate portfolio of Kuwait Finance House in December 1991.</p>
<p>Slight discrepancies in totals are due to rounding.</p>
<p>($1 = 0.302 dinar)</p>
<p>-- Inal Ersan, +965 243-1920</p>
